gateway/node_modules/

# The signer WASM is NOT tracked. It used to be, so that npm shipped a reviewed
# binary rather than whatever the publisher had built locally — but core/types
# and core/crypto are linked into it, so ordinary chain work kept leaving a
# committed binary that no longer matched its source. `prepack` now builds it
# under the toolchain build.sh pins (reproducible: same source, same bytes) and
# re-pins sqc.networks.json, so publishing cannot ship a stale signer either.
